WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.376 --> 00:00:17.838
and Dickon worked in the secret garden all morning.

2
00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:21.840
When Mary went inside for lunch, she ate quickly.

3
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:26.904
"Tell Colin I can't come right now," she said to Martha.

4
00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:30.286
"I'm too busy working in the garden with Dickon."

5
00:00:31.587 --> 00:00:32.588
Martha looked frightened.

6
00:00:34.172 --> 00:00:36.334
"Oh, that will put him in a bad mood."

7
00:00:37.975 --> 00:00:39.116
But Mary didn't care.

8
00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:45.120
She ran back to the secret garden, where Dickon was digging with his own shovel.

9
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:47.661
They worked all afternoon.

10
00:00:48.922 --> 00:00:50.683
The fox and crow were busy too.

11
00:00:52.445 --> 00:00:55.727
Sometimes the crow flapped its wings and flew out of the garden.

12
00:00:56.888 --> 00:01:02.351
Each time it returned, it perched near Dickon and cawed as if it were telling them about its

13
00:01:02.411 --> 00:01:09.507
adventures. When Mary wanted to rest a bit, Dickon sat down with her under a tree.

14
00:01:10.828 --> 00:01:12.909
He took out his pipe and began to play.

15
00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:17.313
Two squirrels appeared on top of the wall to watch and listen.

16
00:01:19.394 --> 00:01:21.436
After a while the children went back to work.

17
00:01:22.997 --> 00:01:26.019
The sun was beginning to set when they finally decided to stop.

18
00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.842
"I'll see you at dawn tomorrow," said Dickon.

19
00:01:31.603 --> 00:01:32.944
Mary ran back to the house.

20
00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:37.582
She could hardly wait to tell Colin about Dickon's fox and crow.

21
00:01:38.842 --> 00:01:41.624
But when Mary arrived at her room, Martha was waiting.

22
00:01:41.644 --> 00:01:44.846
"I wish you'd gone to see Colin today.

23
00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.668
He's been on the verge of a tantrum all afternoon."

24
00:01:50.429 --> 00:01:51.990
Mary pinched her lips together.

25
00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:57.392
She saw no reason why a bad-tempered boy should interfere with what she enjoyed.

26
00:01:58.753 --> 00:02:01.034
She marched down the corridor in a sour mood.

27
00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:05.922
When she entered his room, Colin was not sitting up on his sofa.

28
00:02:07.323 --> 00:02:09.064
Instead he was lying in bed.

29
00:02:09.084 --> 00:02:12.227
"Why are you in bed?"

30
00:02:12.247 --> 00:02:17.972
"I got up this morning when I thought you were coming," Colin said without looking at her.

31
00:02:17.992 --> 00:02:22.095
"This afternoon I asked the servants to put me back in bed.

32
00:02:23.437 --> 00:02:26.299
My back ached and my head ached and I was tired.

33
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.361
Why didn't you come?"

34
00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:33.480
"I was working in the garden with Dickon."

35
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.141
Colin frowned.

36
00:02:34.161 --> 00:02:38.244
"I won't let that boy in here if you stay with him instead of coming to talk to

37
00:02:38.304 --> 00:02:41.206
me." Now Mary was angry.

38
00:02:42.606 --> 00:02:45.609
"If you do that, I'll never come into this room again."

39
00:02:45.629 --> 00:02:48.430
"You'll have to if I want you to."

40
00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.892
"I won't!"

41
00:02:51.412 --> 00:02:52.613
Mary stamped her foot.

42
00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:54.514
"I'll make you.

43
00:02:54.935 --> 00:02:55.875
They'll drag you in."

44
00:02:55.895 --> 00:02:58.157
"Will they, Mr.

45
00:02:58.217 --> 00:03:02.420
Rajah? They can drag me in, but they can't make me talk!

46
00:03:03.724 --> 00:03:06.465
I'll sit and clench my teeth and never tell you one thing.

47
00:03:07.745 --> 00:03:08.746
I won't even look at you.

48
00:03:09.146 --> 00:03:10.346
I'll stare at the floor!"

49
00:03:12.107 --> 00:03:13.227
They glared at each other.

50
00:03:13.247 --> 00:03:15.988
"You're a selfish thing!"

51
00:03:16.448 --> 00:03:17.208
cried Colin.

52
00:03:18.649 --> 00:03:20.829
Mary's eyes flashed with fire.

53
00:03:20.849 --> 00:03:22.190
"And so are you!"

54
00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:25.911
"I'm not as selfish as your perfect Dickon is.

55
00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:29.272
He keeps you outside when I need you here.

56
00:03:31.048 --> 00:03:33.910
And I'm not as selfish as you are because I'm always ill.

57
00:03:35.331 --> 00:03:38.633
I'm sure there's a lump coming on my back, and I'm going to die!"

58
00:03:38.653 --> 00:03:41.215
"Oh, you are not!"

59
00:03:42.636 --> 00:03:44.437
Colin opened his eyes wide.

60
00:03:45.898 --> 00:03:48.179
No one had ever said anything like that to him.

61
00:03:50.041 --> 00:03:51.021
"You know I am!"

62
00:03:51.442 --> 00:03:51.842
he said.

63
00:03:51.862 --> 00:03:54.444
"Everybody says so."

64
00:03:54.464 --> 00:03:58.246
"You just say that to make people feel sorry for you.

65
00:03:59.607 --> 00:04:00.788
I believe you're proud of it."

66
00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:05.282
In spite of his bad back, Colin sat up in bed.

67
00:04:05.302 --> 00:04:08.084
"Get out of this room!"

68
00:04:08.644 --> 00:04:10.165
He threw his pillow at her.

69
00:04:10.185 --> 00:04:13.728
"I'm going, and I won't come back."

70
00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:17.851
She walked to the door, but then she turned around.

71
00:04:17.871 --> 00:04:23.274
"I was going to tell you all sorts of nice things about Dickon's fox and crow.

72
00:04:24.575 --> 00:04:26.396
But now I won't tell you anything."

73
00:04:27.737 --> 00:04:29.178
She stormed back to her room.

74
00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:34.469
Martha was waiting for her, but this time the housemaid was smiling.

75
00:04:34.489 --> 00:04:36.390
"Look what Mr.

76
00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:37.350
Craven sent!"

77
00:04:38.731 --> 00:04:42.552
There on the table was a wooden box full of neatly wrapped packages.

78
00:04:44.053 --> 00:04:45.634
Mary sat down and opened them.

79
00:04:46.994 --> 00:04:51.876
Mr. Craven had sent her picture books and games and a beautiful pen and inkstand.

80
00:04:53.597 --> 00:04:57.518
If she hadn't been fighting with Colin, she would have run to show him everything.

81
00:04:58.839 --> 00:05:01.040
They would have read the books and played with the games.

82
00:05:02.508 --> 00:05:07.191
He would have enjoyed himself so much, he would have forgotten all about checking for lumps.

83
00:05:08.652 --> 00:05:13.514
"He always begins to think about that when he's tired or upset," Mary said to herself.

84
00:05:15.175 --> 00:05:16.136
"He's upset today.

85
00:05:17.357 --> 00:05:19.918
Maybe he's been thinking about his back all afternoon."

86
00:05:21.279 --> 00:05:22.820
She looked at her pile of presents.

87
00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:27.422
"I said I'd never go back, but maybe I'll go in the morning."

88
00:05:28.783 --> 00:05:32.503
She'd try to see him—even if he did throw his pillow at her again.
